      "side": 1,
      "message": "no, doing thousands of unverified I2C transfers is not more robust.\nIt might allow to paper over a PS875 issue, but a small fraction of them will always fail and make VBUS virtually flap.\n\nOverall VBUS level is polled fairly often, making it 3 or 4 order of magnitudes slower is not necessarily the best strategy, maybe PPC interrupt is still not a thing, but here it\u0027s a net regression.",
