      "side": 1,
      "message": "I corrected the unverified part (CL:995959), thanks again for spotting that.\n\nCaching is inherently prone to getting out of sync with reality, especially if you are having trouble getting the correct interrupts. Timing this read on a 400kHz bus takes around ~350usec for the tcpc i2c read to return. Is ~350us not worth having an invalid cache state? (When a cable is plugged in, we call get_vbus_level about ~5/sec). Let me know your thoughts.",
